# Unity Project Instructions

Prioritize token efficiency.

- Do not run terminal commands unless they are necessary to complete the task.

- Do not run shell commands merely to verify that an edit succeeded.

- Do not attempt to build or run the Unity project from the terminal after normal code edits.

- Do not repeatedly inspect files that have already been read unless they changed.

- Read only files relevant to the current task.

- Prefer targeted code search over broad repository exploration.

- Do not scan the entire Assets directory unless explicitly requested.

- Do not inspect Library, Temp, Logs, Obj, Builds, or generated Unity files.

- Make the requested changes directly when the necessary context is already available.

- Keep explanations concise.

- Do not summarize every edit unless requested.

- When debugging, inspect the specific error and related files before exploring unrelated code.

- If Unity Editor execution is required to verify something, tell me what needs to be tested instead of attempting extensive terminal-based verification.